{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's arrival at the pickup is corroborated by the GPS trace and does not rest on his app button alone: the nearest fix is 2.73 m from the Block 512, Bedok North Street 3 pickup coordinate, with a reported accuracy of 5 m, which is inside the STANDARD zone arrival radius of 50 m and inside the 120 s corroboration window, and the arrival check on this trace returns corroborated = true. Both EV-TRIP-05052 and EV-GPS-05052 are COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so this finding is unimpaired.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052", "EV-GPS-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-GPS-05052.payload.derived.v7.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The free wait was served in full. This was an on-demand booking with scheduled_at null, so under POL-NS-21 the 300 s free wait runs from the driver's arrival at 19:31:00 and expires at 19:36:00. The driver cancelled at 19:37:20 — 380 s after arrival and 75 s after the platform's own wait timer expired at 19:36:05 — so the free-wait precondition for cancelling as a rider no-show is satisfied on the trip record with time to spare.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-TRIP-05052.payload.derived.v7.free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on this record puts the wait at the driver's door. He was assigned at 19:23:05, began navigating at 19:23:11 and arrived at 19:31:00, and the only external artifact for this trip — the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05052-01 — is MISSING, issues [MISSING_ARTIFACT], weight 0.0, so no advisory is on file and there is no evidenced delay to excuse the rider's absence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052", "EV-ADVIS-05052-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The amount charged is exactly the policy amount. The payments ledger carries a single cancellation-fee line of 5.00 SGD, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0, and fee_matches_policy = true. Under POL-NS-22 that fee is payable to the driver as compensation for time and fuel where it stands, so on the substantive no-show test the record supports DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both at 5.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05052", "EV-TRIP-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-FARE-05052.payload.derived.money",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome must be read off this filer. The rider filed (filed_by RIDER) and the 5.00 SGD is still charged with no refund issued, so under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION is party-relative and preserves the present payment state — it leaves the fee with the driver and records that the rider's claim as filed is not supported. NO_ACTION never means restoring a charge; here it is simply the fee standing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05052", "EV-TRIP-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-FARE-05052.payload.refund_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's excuse for not coming down — that she was 'in the lift with no signal' — is contradicted by the chat log. The platform delivered both driver messages and records the rider reading them at 19:31:40 and 19:34:23, both before the 19:37:20 cancellation; her only reply came at 19:38:05, 45 s after the trip was cancelled. She therefore had connectivity during the free wait, was alerted that the driver was at the void deck, and chose not to come down until after the driver had waited the full period and left.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05052", "EV-TRIP-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-CHAT-05052.payload.messages.read_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's other route to a refund, driver no-show under POL-NS-24, does not open on this record: this is an on-demand trip with no scheduled pickup time, so there is no 'scheduled pickup time plus 5 minutes' to measure the driver against, and in any event the driver arrived 7 min 55 s after being assigned and waited the full free period.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052", "EV-GPS-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-TRIP-05052.payload.derived.v7.driver_deadline",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Candidly, the contact obligation is the one limb the record does not carry in full. Under POL-NS-23 the driver must have sent at least one in-app message AND placed at least one in-app call before cancelled_at. The message half is met and is admitted on both sides — two in-app messages at 19:31:30 and 19:34:10, both before cancellation, both read by the rider — but trip_record.in_app_calls is empty and the chat log's three contiguous entries are all in-app text with no voice-call entry, so the call half is not evidenced on EV-TRIP-05052 or EV-CHAT-05052. The driver does not overstate the point: his case for keeping the fee rests on the corroborated arrival, the served free wait and the correct 5.00 SGD fee, not on the contact limb.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05052", "EV-CHAT-05052"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-TRIP-05052.payload.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
